# Local-only secrets for the R2 S3 API (Implementation Brief 014) — copy this
# file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in real values ONLY if you want
# to exercise a real presigned-upload round trip against a real (small,
# dev-only) R2 bucket locally. Without this file, presigned URL generation
# still runs (aws4fetch needs no network to sign a URL), it just won't work
# against a real R2 endpoint — every other part of the upload flow (D1
# metadata, the /upload-complete verification against Miniflare's local R2
# emulation, the admin UI) works without any of this. See
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md "R2 credentials" for staging/production, which use
# `wrangler secret put` instead — never a file.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Contact form (Production Readiness Step 1) — RESEND_API_KEY is a real
# secret, never committed (see wrangler.toml's "Contact form" comment).
# Without it, sendContactEmail's real Resend call fails closed (a 401);
# every other part of the flow (validation, Turnstile with the committed
# test keys, rate limiting) still works locally without this. Get a key at
# https://resend.com/api-keys — the default `onboarding@resend.dev` sender
# already configured in wrangler.toml's local [vars] works with any Resend
# account, no domain verification needed, for local testing only.
RESEND_API_KEY=
